.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness-vm-shutdown - Gracefully shut down a harness VM


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness vm shutdown <target-id> <vmid> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Gracefully shut down a harness VM. With neither --timeout nor --force-stop
this drives pveforge's idempotent VMShutdown (a no-op if already stopped,
refuses a paused guest). With either flag it issues PVE's status/shutdown
directly, since the idempotent op cannot express them.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--force-stop\fP[=false]
	let PVE hard-stop the VM if the graceful shutdown times out

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for shutdown

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--pool\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness pool a VM must be a member of

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness tag a VM must carry

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0
	seconds PVE waits for the guest before giving up (0 = PVE default)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-harness-vm(1)\fP
